<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viking Age</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 793–1066</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> Age is the period from the late 8th to the mid 11th century in which Scandinavians raided, traded and settled across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the North Atlantic. Its beginning is usually dated to the raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> in 793 and its end to 1066. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> itself it saw the growth of trading towns, the first kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, and conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viking-age.jpg" alt="Viking Age" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: historical museum · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bildsten_fr%C3%A5n_Smiss,_Gotland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
